 "title": "The Arda Basin Partnership (invented)",
 "about": "An invented partnership of three riparian states, a basin commission, a development bank, two cities and the delta's fishers for clean water in a river basin. Every party, figure, decision and vote is invented and said to be; it shows each part of the work. The affairs (ADR 0134) are invented too: the Steering Committee's rule and its two questions, the dry-season negotiation in four drafts, the events between the states with their reports, the secretariat's mandates, two cycles of peer review, and the institutions the parties belong to with what they gave one another.",
